    "note": "Full Phra Pin-klao Bridge: three haunched concrete river spans, two large chamfered-foot river piers, both land approach viaducts, six-lane road/median/painted markings, main-river cantilever pedestrian walks, four mapped stair descents including western switchbacks, slim light-gray rails and paired curved streetlights. Preserve the independent lower Phra Athit crossing. Fixed3m model datum. Approximate overall deck ranges8.4..18.4m above sea level, with elevated approaches and a shallow river crown. Standard review water samples 3.346m. Photo-led haunch/pier/stair sections and standard-terrain fit elevations are visualization controls, not surveyed engineering dimensions. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
